<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Research and software</p>
  <h1 id="page-title">SEDA</h1>
  <p class="lede">Software for Evolving Digital Art.</p>
  <p>
    SEDA explores tools and practices for preserving network-interactive and evolving
    digital art, with a focus on Tezos-based crypto-art and the long-term
    care of works whose behavior depends on code, APIs, storage, and network context.
  </p>
  <p class="status">
    SEDA brings together research, software, and infrastructure work for the
    preservation of evolving digital art.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="cards" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Current anchor</p>
    <h2 id="projects-title">Projects</h2>
  </div>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>ARKIVO.ART</h3>
    <p>
      ARKIVO is an alpha preservation platform for network-interactive and evolving
      crypto-art. It catalogs selected Tezos OBJKTs, captures snapshots, and documents
      artwork behavior for future conservation work.
    </p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://arkivo.art" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit ARKIVO.ART</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>seda-studio on GitHub</h3>
    <p>
      Public repositories for SEDA-related software, including ARKIVO and experimental
      preservation-node tooling.
    </p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/seda-studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View GitHub organization</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>Research foundation</h3>
    <p>
      ARKIVO builds on Daniel Filipe Farinha's PhD research into information systems
      for preserving networked crypto-art.
    </p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15284346" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the thesis</a></p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h3>Post-doctoral research</h3>
    <p>
      SEDA Nodes is a 2026 post-doctoral research project at the Faculty of Arts
      and Humanities of the University of Porto, and a case study for the Teia
      Platform (<a class="text-link" href="https://teia.art" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">teia.art</a>) on Tezos.
    </p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/post-doc/">Read about the post-doc</a></p>
  </article>
</section>

